      "text": "# Safe Offline Archive Importer\n\n## Design Overview\n\nThis implementation provides a secure, robust ZIP archive importer that addresses common security vulnerabilities and reliability concerns when extracting archives from untrusted sources. The key design principles are:\n\n1. **Path Normalization & Traversal Prevention**: Reject any entry whose normalized path escapes the target directory.\n2. **Symlink/Hardlink Safety**: Never create symlinks or hardlinks during extraction; treat them as regular files or reject them.\n3. **Size Limits**: Enforce maximum uncompressed size, compressed size, and total archive size to prevent zip bombs.\n4. **Streaming Extraction**: Process entries one at a time without loading entire archives into memory.\n5. **Atomic Publication**: Extract to a temporary directory, then atomically rename to the final destination.\n6. **Interrupted Extraction Handling**: Use journaling/checkpointing so partial extractions can be detected and cleaned up.\n7. **No External Dependencies**: Pure Python, no reliance on system `unzip` or external tools.\n\n## Security Threats Addressed\n\n| Threat | Mitigation |\n|--------|-----------|\n| Path traversal (`../../etc/passwd`) | Normalize paths, reject absolute paths, reject `..` components |\n| Zip bomb (huge uncompressed size) | Enforce per-entry and total size limits |\n| Symlink attacks | Never create symlinks; reject entries with symlink attributes |\n| Hardlink attacks | Never create hardlinks |\n| Partial extraction corruption | Atomic rename after full extraction; cleanup on failure |\n| Resource exhaustion | Streaming I/O, bounded buffers, size caps |\n| TOCTOU races | Extract to temp dir, verify, then atomic move |\n\n## Implementation\n\n```python\n\"\"\"\nSafe offline archive importer for ZIP files.\n\nThis module provides a secure, streaming ZIP extractor that prevents\npath traversal, zip bombs, symlink attacks, and handles interrupted\nextractions gracefully.\n\nSecurity model:\n- All paths are normalized and validated against the target directory.\n- Symlinks and hardlinks are never created.\n- Size limits are enforced per-entry and globally.\n- Extraction is atomic: temp dir -> verify -> rename.\n- Interrupted extractions leave a marker file for detection/cleanup.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport binascii\nimport io\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport stat\nimport struct\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport threading\nimport time\nimport warnings\nfrom pathlib import Path, PurePosixPath, PureWindowsPath\n\n# Try to import compression modules\ntry:\n    import zlib\n    crc32 = zlib.crc32\nexcept ImportError:\n    zlib = None\n    crc32 = binascii.crc32\n\ntry:\n    import bz2\nexcept ImportError:\n    bz2 = None\n\ntry:\n    import lzma\nexcept ImportError:\n    lzma = None\n\ntry:\n    from compression import zstd\nexcept ImportError:\n    zstd = None\n\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"SafeZipImporter\",\n    \"ImportError\",\n    \"PathTraversalError\",\n    \"ZipBombError\",\n    \"SymlinkError\",\n    \"ExtractionInterruptedError\",\n    \"ArchiveTooLargeError\",\n    \"DEFAULT_MAX_ENTRY_SIZE\",\n    \"DEFAULT_MAX_TOTAL_SIZE\",\n    \"DEFAULT_MAX_ENTRIES\",\n]\n\n\nclass ImportError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for archive import errors.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass PathTraversalError(ImportError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an archive entry attempts to escape the target directory.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass ZipBombError(ImportError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an archive exceeds configured size limits.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass SymlinkError(ImportError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when an archive contains symlink or hardlink entries.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass ExtractionInterruptedError(ImportError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a previous extraction was interrupted and not cleaned up.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass ArchiveTooLargeError(ImportError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when the archive file itself exceeds the maximum allowed size.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\n# Default limits\nDEFAULT_MAX_ENTRY_SIZE = 100 * 1024 * 1024       # 100 MB per entry\nDEFAULT_MAX_TOTAL_SIZE = 1 * 1024 * 1024 * 1024   # 1 GB total uncompressed\nDEFAULT_MAX_ENTRIES = 10000                        # Max number of entries\nDEFAULT_MAX_ARCHIVE_SIZE = 500 * 1024 * 1024       # 500 MB archive file size\n\n# ZIP constants\nZIP_STORED = 0\nZIP_DEFLATED = 8\nZIP_BZIP2 = 12\nZIP_LZMA = 14\nZIP_ZSTANDARD = 93\n\n# End of central directory\n",
